                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I've been playing this game for a while. This game is overwhelmingly vast with a story mostly in the background. Firsts are always going to be very exciting in this game, from discovering your first Earthlike world, Ammonia world, Black hole, Neutron star, getting your first kill, making your first million, then your first billion, unlocking the federal corvette and the imperial cutter, to finally purchasing a fleet carrier. \n\nPros:\n-This game is a grind and the grind can be very rewarding.\n-Sound design is exquisite\n-This game is vast so getting your bonus for first discovery won't be too difficult\n-This game understands scale. All the ships look their size and are good at reminding you of just how small you are\n-This game has really good vr support***\n-System colonization is very good, very rewarding, and really lets Frontier's Tycoon side shine.\n-The game is reasonably priced. \n-The game, while not the best optimized at times, is relatively easy to run mostly due to the fact its old.\n-The story of the game, while mostly background, is pretty interesting.\n-Operations is properly punishing and highly rewards engineering and highly incentivizes unlocking all engineers and playing the game further, while rewarding you greatly.\n-Community goals are VERY profitable and give good access to the general story and lore.\n-The astropolitics are just as bullshit as they would be irl.\n\n\nCons:\n-The astropolitics are just as bullshit as they would be irl.\n-You MUST own Odyssey to enjoy this game to its full potential (not that big of a con but mostly because some core game mechanics are locked behind this dlc and you'll also be locked to the legacy ships if you don't buy any of the dlc)\n-The antialiasing is ABYSMAL and pretty much nonexistent. \n-On a related note to the last point, Odyssey is the least optimized part of the game by a longshot. Sure they've done *some* optimizations but the second you put super sampling to normal it was enough to bring my old 5060ti to its knees begging for death and even gives my 5080 a run for its money at 1440p.\n-***VR DOES NOT WORK ON FOOT. Idk why vr is not compatible on foot. Works just fine in an srv and in ship so I guess just don't do vr if you do exobiology or ground combat.\n-The whole conversation about its \"3 months early access\" model for its new ships just being pay to win. \n-This game WILL crash 4/5 times after about an hour of play and it will crash HARD. \n-If you want a stable experience just make a habit to restart the game every few hours, the graphics will hard glitch out if the game is running for more than 6-12 hours and will reduce the galaxy map to nothing but a couple of gold and blue streaks in the skybox and turn stars in to jumbled messes of light and texture, honestly quite terrifying.\n\nI love this game but patience is a necessity to enjoy the game to its full potential",
